    "hit@5": 1.0,
    "mrr@5": 1.0
   },
   "answer_seconds": 0.906,
   "answer": {
    "text": "Self-attention layers have a per-layer complexity of $O(n^2 \\cdot d)$, while recurrent layers have a complexity of $O(n \\cdot d^2)$ [p. 6](#page=6). Self-attention layers are faster than recurrent layers when the sequence length $n$ is smaller than the representation dimensionality $d$ [p. 6](#page=6).",
